":1,"father":"Shimei","mother":"","v":[4]},{"id":"joah_1623","name":"Joah","also":"","summary":"One of the sons of Obed-edom (1 Chr. 26:4), a Korhite porter.","verses":1,"father":"Shimei","mother":"","v":[4]},{"id":"nethaneel_2192","name":"Nethaneel","also":"","summary":"A temple porter, of the family of the Korhites (1 Chr. 26:4).","verses":1,"father":"Shimei","mother":"","v":[4]},{"id":"sacar_2453","name":"Sacar","also":"","summary":"A son of Obed-edom the Gittite, and a temple porter (1 Chr. 26:4).","verses":1,"father":"Shimei","mother":"","v":[4]},{"id":"ammiel_222","name":"Ammiel","also":"","summary":"One of the sons of Obed-edom the Levite (1 Chr. 26:5).","verses":1,"father":"Shimei","mother":"","v":[5]},{"id":"issachar_646","name":"Issachar","also":"","summary":"Jacob's ninth son.","verses":1,"father":"Shimei","mother":"","v":[5]},{"id":"peulthai_2324","name":"Peulthai","also":"","summary":"Wages of the Lord, one of the sons of Obed-edom, a Levite porter (1 Chr. 26:5).","verses":1,"father":"Shimei","mother":"","v":[5]},{"id":"elihu_1128","name":"Elihu","also":"","summary":"One of the family of Obed-edom, who were appointed porters of the temple under David (1 Chr. 26:7).","verses":1,"father":"Shemaiah","mother":"","v":[7]},{"id":"elzabad_1188","name":"Elzabad","also":"","summary":"Korahite Gatekeeper.","verses":1,"father":"Shemaiah","mother":"","v":[7]},{"id":"obed_2231","name":"Obed","also":"","summary":"1 Chr. 26:7.","verses":1,"father":"Shemaiah","mother":"","v":[7]},{"id":"othni_2258","name":"Othni","also":"","summary":"A lion of Jehovah, a son of Shemaiah, and one of the temple porters in the time of David (1 Chr. 26:7).","verses":1,"father":"Shemaiah","mother":"","v":[7]},{"id":"rephael_2421","name":"Rephael","also":"","summary":"Healed of God, one of Shemaiah’s sons.","verses":1,"father":"Shemaiah","mother":"","v":[7]},{"id":"semachiah_2487","name":"Semachiah","also":"","summary":"","verses":1,"father":"Shemaiah","mother":"","v":[7]},{"id":"merari_2004","name":"Merari","also":"","summary":"Sad; bitter, the youngest son of Levi, born before the descent of Jacob into Egypt, and one of the seventy who accompanied him thither (Gen. 46:11; Ex. 6:16).","verses":38,"father":"Levi","mother":"","v":[10,19]},{"id":"hosah_1554","name":"Hosah","also":"","summary":"A Levite of the family of Merari (1 Chr. 16:38).","verses":4,"father":"","mother":"","v":[10,11,16]},{"id":"simri_2754","name":"Simri","also":"","summary":"Watchman, a Levite of the family of Merari (1 Chr. 26:10).","verses":1,"father":"Hosah","mother":"","v":[10]},{"id":"hilkiah_1526","name":"Hilkiah","also":"","summary":"1 Chr. 26:11.","verses":1,"father":"Hosah","mother":"","v":[11]},{"id":"tebaliah_2833","name":"Tebaliah","also":"","summary":"","verses":1,"father":"Hosah","mother":"","v":[11]},{"id":"zechariah_3006","name":"Zechariah","also":"","summary":"","verses":1,"father":"Hosah","mother":"","v":[11]},{"id":"shuppim_2733","name":"Shuppim","also":"","summary":"Hosah.","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[16]},{"id":"ahijah_139","name":"Ahijah","also":"","summary":"A Levite having charge of the sacred treasury in the temple (1 Chr. 26:20).","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[20]},{"id":"laadan_1823","name":"Laadan","also":"Libni, Jahath","summary":"White, one of the two sons of Gershon, the son of Levi (Ex. 6:17; Num. 3:18, 21).","verses":9,"father":"Gershon","mother":"","v":[21]},{"id":"jehiel_771","name":"Jehiel","also":"Jehieli","summary":"The sons of Ladan.","verses":4,"father":"","mother":"","v":[21,22]},{"id":"joel_1655","name":"Joel","also":"","summary":"Sons of Ladan.","verses":2,"father":"Jehiel","mother":"","v":[22]},{"id":"zetham_3056","name":"Zetham","also":"","summary":"Olive planter, a Levite (1 Chr. 23:8).","verses":2,"father":"Jehiel","mother":"","v":[22]},{"id":"moses_2108","name":"Moses","also":"","summary":"Drawn (or Egypt. mesu, “son;” hence Rameses, royal son). On the invitation of Pharaoh (Gen. 45:17-25), Jacob and his sons went down into Egypt.","verses":774,"father":"Amram","mother":"Jochebed","v":[24]},{"id":"gershom_1302","name":"Gershom","also":"","summary":"The elder of the two sons of Moses born to him in Midian (Ex. 2:22; 18:3). On his way to Egypt with his family, in obedience to the command of the Lord, Moses was attacked by a sudden and dangerous illness (4:24-26), which Zipporah his wife believed to have been sent because he had neglected to circumcise his son.","verses":5,"father":"Moses","mother":"Zipporah","v":[24]},{"id":"shubael_2579","name":"Shubael","also":"Shebuel","summary":"One of the descendants of Gershom, who had charge of the temple treasures in the time of David (1 Chr. 23:16; 26:24).","verses":3,"father":"Gershom","mother":"","v":[24]},{"id":"eliezer_1114","name":"Eliezer","also":"","summary":"One of the two sons of Moses, born during his sojourn in Midian (Ex. 18:4; 1 Chr. 23:15, 17). He remained with his mother and brother Gershom with Jethro when Moses returned to Egypt.","verses":4,"father":"Moses","mother":"Zipporah","v":[25]},{"id":"rehabiah_2409","name":"Rehabiah","also":"","summary":"Enlargement of the Lord, the son of Eliezer, and grandson of Moses (1 Chr. 23:17; 24:21).","verses":3,"father":"Eliezer","mother":"","v":[25]},{"id":"shelomith_2609","name":"Shelomith","also":"","summary":"Son of Zichri.","verses":3,"father":"Zichri","mother":"","v":[25,26,28]},{"id":"jeshaiah_647","name":"Jeshaiah","also":"Isshiah","summary":"A Kohathite Levite, the father of Joram, of the family of Eliezer (1 Chr. 26:25); called also Isshiah (24:21).","verses":2,"father":"Rehabiah","mother":"","v":[25]},{"id":"joram_1706","name":"Joram","also":"","summary":"Son of Ahab.","verses":1,"father":"Jeshaiah","mother":"","v":[25]},{"id":"zichri_3070","name":"Zichri","also":"","summary":"","verses":1,"father":"Joram","mother":"","v":[25]},{"id":"david_994","name":"David","also":"","summary":"Beloved, the eighth and youngest son of Jesse, a citizen of Bethlehem. His father seems to have been a man in humble life. His mother’s name is not recorded.","verses":896,"father":"Jesse","mother":"","v":[26,31,32]},{"id":"samuel_2469","name":"Samuel","also":"Shemuel","summary":"Heard of God. The peculiar circumstances connected with his birth are recorded in 1 Sam. 1:20. Hannah, one of the two wives of Elkanah, who came up to Shiloh to worship before the Lord, earnestly prayed to God that she might become the mother of a son.","verses":122,"father":"Elkanah","mother":"Hannah","v":[28]},{"id":"joab_1617","name":"Joab","also":"","summary":"One of the three sons of Zeruiah, David’s sister, and “captain of the host” during the whole of David’s reign (2 Sam. 2:13; 10:7; 11:1; 1 Kings 11:15).","verses":119,"father":"","mother":"Zeruiah","v":[28]},{"id":"abner_57","name":"Abner","also":"","summary":"Father of light; i.e., “enlightening”, the son of Ner and uncle of Saul. He was commander-in-chief of Saul’s army (1 Sam. 14:50; 17:55; 20:25).","verses":53,"father":"Ner","mother":"","v":[28]},{"id":"zeruiah_3055","name":"Zeruiah","also":"","summary":"Stricken of the Lord, David’s sister, and the mother of Abishai, Joab, and Asahel (1 Chr. 2:16), who were the three leading heroes of David’s army, and being his nephews, they were admitted to the closest companionship with him.","verses":25,"father":"Nahash","mother":"","v":[28]},{"id":"ner_2181","name":"Ner","also":"","summary":"Light, the father of Kish (1 Chr. 8:33). 1 Sam. 14:51 should be read, “Kish, the father of Saul, and Ner, the father of Abner, were the sons of Abiel.”","verses":14,"father":"Abiel","mother":"Maachah","v":[28]},{"id":"kish_1784","name":"Kish","also":"Cis","summary":"A Benjamite, the son of Abiel, and father of king Saul (1 Sam. 9:1, 3; 10:11, 21; 14:51; 2 Sam. 21:14). All that is recorded of him is that he sent his son Saul in search of his asses that had strayed, and that he was buried in Zelah.","verses":13,"father":"Abiel","mother":"Maachah","v":[28]},{"id":"chenaniah_936","name":"Chenaniah","also":"","summary":"Chief Levite when David brought up the ark from the house of Obed-Edom.","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[29]},{"id":"hashabiah_1431","name":"Hashabiah","also":"","summary":"","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[30]},{"id":"jerijah_863","name":"Jerijah","also":"","summary":"","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[31]},{"id":"manasseh_1928","name":"Manasseh","also":"Manasses","summary":"The elder of the two sons of Joseph. He and his brother Ephraim were afterwards adopted by Jacob as his own sons (48:1).","verses":109,"father":"Joseph","mother":"Asenath","v":[32]}],"places":[{"id":"shallecheth_1059","name":"Shallecheth","kind":"Landmark (Gate)","lat":31.77744,"lon":35.23494,"summary":"I.e., “the gate of casting out,” hence supposed to be the refuse gate; one of the gates of the house of the Lord, “by the causeway of the going up” i.e., the causeway rising up from the Tyropoeon valley = valley of the cheesemakers (1 Chr. 26:16).","verses":1,"v":[16]},{"id":"parbar_1296","name":"Parbar","kind":"Landmark","lat":31.77667,"lon":35.23417,"summary":"Added from Digital Manna places-1275 (LPF sync 2026-10-13)","verses":1,"v":[18]},{"id":"jordan_653","name":"Jordan","kind":"Water (River)","lat":33.18645,"lon":35.61916,"summary":"But besides these two historical fountains there is a third, called the Hasbany, which rises in the bottom of a valley at the western base of Hermon, 12 miles north of Tell-el-Kady.","verses":177,"v":[30]},{"id":"gilead_475","name":"Gilead","kind":"Region","lat":32.75,"lon":35.75,"summary":"Hill of testimony, (Gen. 31:21), a mountainous region east of Jordan. From its mountainous character it is called “the mount of Gilead” (Gen. 31:25).","verses":80,"v":[31]},{"id":"jazer_628","name":"Jazer","kind":"City","lat":31.94353,"lon":35.72777,"summary":"He (God) helps, a city of the Amorites on the east of Jordan, and assigned, with neighbouring places in Gilead, to Gad (Num. 32:1, 35; Josh. 13:25).","verses":12,"v":[31